IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc2-prohibited-acts.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), PART II, ss 49 to 56 ("Prohibited Acts"): assisting an alien enemy or omitting to prevent treason,
-- intimidating Parliament, sabotage (ss 52 to 52.3), inciting to mutiny, assisting a deserter, evidence of overt acts, offences in relation to members of the R.C.M.P.
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively). Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30);
-- it is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words) / NOTHING (not covered): see the header of ccc2-treason.l4 and NOTES.md.
-- Where a section states only "guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction", the penalty is s 787(1)'s: it is a seam INPUT (PLAN.md section 6, ccc2 row).

§ `Section 49 -- repealed`

-- src:889 | Prohibited Acts
-- src:890 | 49 [Repealed, 2018, c. 29, s. 1]
@ref Criminal Code s 49 (repealed) (src:889-890)
`s 49 as the text shows it` MEANS "49 [Repealed, 2018, c. 29, s. 1]"

§ `Section 50 -- Assisting alien enemy to leave Canada, or omitting to prevent treason`

-- src:891 | Assisting alien enemy to leave Canada, or omitting to prevent treason
-- src:892 | 50 (1) Every one commits an offence who
-- src:893 | (a) incites or wilfully assists a subject of
-- src:894 | (i) a state that is at war with Canada, or
-- src:895 | (ii) a state against whose forces Canadian Forces are engaged in hostilities, whether or not a state of war exists between Canada and the state whose forces they are,
-- src:896 | to leave Canada without the consent of the Crown, unless the accused establishes that assistance to the state referred to in subparagraph (i) or the forces of the state referred to in subparagraph (ii), as the case may be, was not intended thereby; or
-- src:897 | (b) knowing that a person is about to commit high treason or treason does not, with all reasonable dispatch, inform a justice of the peace or other peace officer thereof or make other reasonable efforts to prevent that person from committing high treason or treason.
@ref Criminal Code s 50(1) (assisting alien enemy to leave Canada, or omitting to prevent treason) (src:891-897)
GIVEN `the person incites, or wilfully assists, a subject of such a state to leave Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the state is one that is at war with Canada, or one against whose forces Canadian Forces are engaged in hostilities, whether or not a state of war exists` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the leaving is without the consent of the Crown` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused establishes that assistance to the state, or to its forces, was not intended thereby` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 50(1)(a) the person assists a subject of an enemy state to leave Canada` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person incites, or wilfully assists, a subject of such a state to leave Canada` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "incites or wilfully assists a subject of"
        IF NOT `the state is one that is at war with Canada, or one against whose forces Canadian Forces are engaged in hostilities, whether or not a state of war exists` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(i) a state that is at war with Canada, or (ii) a state against whose forces Canadian Forces are engaged in hostilities"
        IF NOT `the leaving is without the consent of the Crown` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without the consent of the Crown"
        IF `the accused establishes that assistance to the state, or to its forces, was not intended thereby` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the accused establishes that assistance to the state referred to in subparagraph (i) or the forces of the state referred to in subparagraph (ii), as the case may be, was not intended thereby"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- Paragraph (b): "does not, with all reasonable dispatch, inform a justice of the peace or other peace officer thereof or make other reasonable efforts to prevent":
-- read as neither informing nor making other reasonable efforts (fork F5). The recipient being "a justice of the peace or other peace officer" is s 2 "peace officer" (a seam input).
@ref Criminal Code s 50(1)(b) (omitting to prevent treason) (src:897)
GIVEN `the person knows that another person is about to commit high treason or treason` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person informed someone of it with all reasonable dispatch` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2 peace officer: the person informed is a justice of the peace or other peace officer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person made other reasonable efforts to prevent that person from committing high treason or treason` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 50(1)(b) the person omits to prevent treason` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person knows that another person is about to commit high treason or treason` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "knowing that a person is about to commit high treason or treason"
        IF `the person made other reasonable efforts to prevent that person from committing high treason or treason` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "or make other reasonable efforts to prevent"
        IF `the person informed someone of it with all reasonable dispatch` AND `s 2 peace officer: the person informed is a justice of the peace or other peace officer` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "inform a justice of the peace or other peace officer"
        IF `the person informed someone of it with all reasonable dispatch` AND `s 2 peace officer: the person informed is a justice of the peace or other peace officer` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 2 "peace officer includes" leaves the informed person's status open
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- The same duty as a regulative rule: the person must inform, or make other reasonable efforts. The text states no time but "with all reasonable dispatch", so no WITHIN is invented.
-- A DEONTIC value cannot be compared with EQUALS in an #ASSERT on the stable binary: the rule is run with #TRACE in the tests file and the decision function above is asserted.
@ref Criminal Code s 50(1)(b) (omitting to prevent treason) (src:897)
DECLARE `s 50(1)(b) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 50(1)(b) informs a justice of the peace or other peace officer`
    `s 50(1)(b) makes other reasonable efforts to prevent the commission of the treason`

@ref Criminal Code s 50(1)(b) (omitting to prevent treason) (src:897)
`s 50(1)(b) the duty to inform or to make other reasonable efforts` MEANS
    (PARTY `the accused`
     MUST `s 50(1)(b) informs a justice of the peace or other peace officer`
     HENCE FULFILLED
     LEST BREACH BY `the accused` BECAUSE "s 50(1)(b): the person did not inform a justice of the peace or other peace officer")
    ROR
    (PARTY `the accused`
     MUST `s 50(1)(b) makes other reasonable efforts to prevent the commission of the treason`
     HENCE FULFILLED
     LEST BREACH BY `the accused` BECAUSE "s 50(1)(b): the person made no other reasonable efforts to prevent the commission of the treason")

