§ `Section 51 -- Intimidating Parliament or legislature`

-- src:900 | Intimidating Parliament or legislature
-- src:901 | 51 Every one who does an act of violence in order to intimidate Parliament or the legislature of a province is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding fourteen years.
@ref Criminal Code s 51 (intimidating Parliament or legislature) (src:900-901)
GIVEN `the person does an act of violence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is in order to intimidate Parliament or the legislature of a province` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 51 the person intimidates Parliament or the legislature of a province` MEANS
    IF `the person does an act of violence` AND `the act is in order to intimidate Parliament or the legislature of a province`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every one who does an act of violence in order to intimidate Parliament or the legislature of a province"

@ref Criminal Code s 51 (punishment) (src:900-901)
`s 51 the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

@ref Criminal Code s 51 (punishment) (src:900-901)
`s 51 the punishment` MEANS
    LIST Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

§ `Section 52 -- Sabotage`

-- Subsection (2): "prohibited act means an act or omission that (a) impairs the efficiency or impedes the working of any vessel, vehicle, aircraft, machinery, apparatus or other thing; or
-- (b) causes property, by whomever it may be owned, to be lost, damaged or destroyed." A "means" definition: an act neither (a) nor (b) is not a prohibited act (JUST FALSE).
-- src:906 | Definition of prohibited act
-- src:907 | (2) In this section, prohibited act means an act or omission that
-- src:908 | (a) impairs the efficiency or impedes the working of any vessel, vehicle, aircraft, machinery, apparatus or other thing; or
-- src:909 | (b) causes property, by whomever it may be owned, to be lost, damaged or destroyed.
@ref Criminal Code s 52(2) (definition of prohibited act) (src:906-909)
GIVEN `the act or omission impairs the efficiency or impedes the working of any vessel, vehicle, aircraft, machinery, apparatus or other thing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act or omission causes property, by whomever it may be owned, to be lost, damaged or destroyed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 52(2) the act or omission is a prohibited act` MEANS
    IF `the act or omission impairs the efficiency or impedes the working of any vessel, vehicle, aircraft, machinery, apparatus or other thing`
        OR `the act or omission causes property, by whomever it may be owned, to be lost, damaged or destroyed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "prohibited act means an act or omission that"

-- Subsection (3): "No person does a prohibited act within the meaning of this section by reason only that (a) he stops work as a result of the failure of his employer and himself to agree
-- on any matter relating to his employment; (b) ... a bargaining agent acting on his behalf ...; or (c) ... a combination of workmen or employees for their own reasonable protection."
-- A flat negative: when the stated ground is the only ground the answer is JUST FALSE; otherwise the subsection is silent (NOTHING).
-- src:910 | Saving
-- src:911 | (3) No person does a prohibited act within the meaning of this section by reason only that
-- src:912 | (a) he stops work as a result of the failure of his employer and himself to agree on any matter relating to his employment;
-- src:913 | (b) he stops work as a result of the failure of his employer and a bargaining agent acting on his behalf to agree on any matter relating to his employment; or
-- src:914 | (c) he stops work as a result of his taking part in a combination of workmen or employees for their own reasonable protection as workmen or employees.
@ref Criminal Code s 52(3) (saving) (src:910-914)
GIVEN `the only reason the act or omission could be a prohibited act is that the person stops work as a result of the failure of the person and their employer to agree on any matter relating to the person's employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 52(3)(a) the person does a prohibited act by reason only of stopping work over a failure to agree with the employer` MEANS
    IF `the only reason the act or omission could be a prohibited act is that the person stops work as a result of the failure of the person and their employer to agree on any matter relating to the person's employment`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person does a prohibited act within the meaning of this section by reason only that (a) he stops work as a result of the failure of his employer and himself to agree on any matter relating to his employment"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection does not speak to any other reason

@ref Criminal Code s 52(3)(b) (saving) (src:910-914)
GIVEN `the only reason the act or omission could be a prohibited act is that the person stops work as a result of the failure of the person's employer and a bargaining agent acting on the person's behalf to agree on any matter relating to the person's employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 52(3)(b) the person does a prohibited act by reason only of stopping work over a failure of the employer and a bargaining agent to agree` MEANS
    IF `the only reason the act or omission could be a prohibited act is that the person stops work as a result of the failure of the person's employer and a bargaining agent acting on the person's behalf to agree on any matter relating to the person's employment`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person does a prohibited act within the meaning of this section by reason only that ... (b) he stops work as a result of the failure of his employer and a bargaining agent acting on his behalf to agree on any matter relating to his employment"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection does not speak to any other reason

@ref Criminal Code s 52(3)(c) (saving) (src:910-914)
GIVEN `the only reason the act or omission could be a prohibited act is that the person stops work as a result of taking part in a combination of workmen or employees for their own reasonable protection as workmen or employees` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 52(3)(c) the person does a prohibited act by reason only of stopping work as a result of taking part in a combination for reasonable protection` MEANS
    IF `the only reason the act or omission could be a prohibited act is that the person stops work as a result of taking part in a combination of workmen or employees for their own reasonable protection as workmen or employees`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person does a prohibited act within the meaning of this section by reason only that ... (c) he stops work as a result of his taking part in a combination of workmen or employees for their own reasonable protection as workmen or employees"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection does not speak to any other reason

