`s 52(4) the person does a prohibited act by reason only of attending at or near a dwelling-house or place to obtain or communicate information` MEANS
    IF `the only reason the act or omission could be a prohibited act is that the person attends at or near or approaches a dwelling-house or place for the purpose only of obtaining or communicating information`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person does a prohibited act within the meaning of this section by reason only that he attends at or near or approaches a dwelling-house or place for the purpose only of obtaining or communicating information"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection does not speak to any other reason

-- Subsection (5): "For greater certainty, no person commits an offence under subsection (1) if they do a prohibited act while participating in advocacy, protest or dissent but they do not
-- intend to cause any of the harms referred to in paragraphs (1)(a) and (b)." A declaratory flat negative (JUST FALSE).
-- src:917 | For greater certainty
-- src:918 | (5) For greater certainty, no person commits an offence under subsection (1) if they do a prohibited act while participating in advocacy, protest or dissent but they do not intend to cause any of the harms referred to in paragraphs (1)(a) and (b).
@ref Criminal Code s 52(5) (for greater certainty) (src:917-918)
GIVEN `the person does a prohibited act while participating in advocacy, protest or dissent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person intends to cause one of the harms referred to in paragraph 52(1)(a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 52(5) the person commits an offence under subsection 52(1) while participating in advocacy, protest or dissent` MEANS
    IF `the person does a prohibited act while participating in advocacy, protest or dissent` AND (NOT `the person intends to cause one of the harms referred to in paragraph 52(1)(a) or (b)`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no person commits an offence under subsection (1) if they do a prohibited act while participating in advocacy, protest or dissent but they do not intend to cause any of the harms"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says no only where the person lacks the intent

-- Subsection (1): "Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years or is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction who does
-- a prohibited act with the intent to endanger (a) the safety, security or defence of Canada, or (b) the safety or security of the naval, army or air forces of any state other than Canada that are
-- lawfully present in Canada." The elements are asked as facts; the prohibited act is worked out by subsection (2), qualified by (3) and (4); (5) is read first.
-- src:902 | Sabotage
-- src:903 | 52 (1) Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years or is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction who does a prohibited act with the intent to endanger
-- src:904 | (a) the safety, security or defence of Canada, or
-- src:905 | (b) the safety or security of the naval, army or air forces of any state other than Canada that are lawfully present in Canada.
-- src:917 | For greater certainty
-- src:918 | (5) For greater certainty, no person commits an offence under subsection (1) if they do a prohibited act while participating in advocacy, protest or dissent but they do not intend to cause any of the harms referred to in paragraphs (1)(a) and (b).
@ref Criminal Code s 52(1) and (5) (sabotage) (src:902-918)
GIVEN `the act or omission impairs the efficiency or impedes the working of any vessel, vehicle, aircraft, machinery, apparatus or other thing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act or omission causes property, by whomever it may be owned, to be lost, damaged or destroyed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the only reason it could be a prohibited act is stopping work over a failure to agree with the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the only reason it could be a prohibited act is stopping work over a failure of the employer and a bargaining agent to agree` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the only reason it could be a prohibited act is stopping work as a result of taking part in a combination for reasonable protection` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the only reason it could be a prohibited act is attending at or near a dwelling-house or place to obtain or communicate information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person participates in advocacy, protest or dissent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person intends to endanger the safety, security or defence of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person intends to endanger the safety or security of the naval, army or air forces of a state other than Canada that are lawfully present in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 52(1) the person commits sabotage` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the prohibited act answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the person participates in advocacy, protest or dissent` AND (NOT `an intent to endanger`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no person commits an offence under subsection (1) if they do a prohibited act while participating in advocacy, protest or dissent but they do not intend to cause any of the harms referred to in paragraphs (1)(a) and (b)" (subsection (5))
        IF `the prohibited act answer` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "prohibited act means an act or omission that" and "No person does a prohibited act within the meaning of this section by reason only that" (subsections (2) to (4))
        IF `the prohibited act answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `an intent to endanger` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "who does a prohibited act with the intent to endanger"
    WHERE
        `an intent to endanger` MEANS
                `the person intends to endanger the safety, security or defence of Canada`
            OR  `the person intends to endanger the safety or security of the naval, army or air forces of a state other than Canada that are lawfully present in Canada`
        `the prohibited act answer` MEANS
            IF    `s 52(3)(a) the person does a prohibited act by reason only of stopping work over a failure to agree with the employer` `the only reason it could be a prohibited act is stopping work over a failure to agree with the employer` EQUALS JUST FALSE
               OR `s 52(3)(b) the person does a prohibited act by reason only of stopping work over a failure of the employer and a bargaining agent to agree` `the only reason it could be a prohibited act is stopping work over a failure of the employer and a bargaining agent to agree` EQUALS JUST FALSE
               OR `s 52(3)(c) the person does a prohibited act by reason only of stopping work as a result of taking part in a combination for reasonable protection` `the only reason it could be a prohibited act is stopping work as a result of taking part in a combination for reasonable protection` EQUALS JUST FALSE
               OR `s 52(4) the person does a prohibited act by reason only of attending at or near a dwelling-house or place to obtain or communicate information` `the only reason it could be a prohibited act is attending at or near a dwelling-house or place to obtain or communicate information` EQUALS JUST FALSE
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person does a prohibited act within the meaning of this section by reason only that" (the flat negatives of subsections (3) and (4))
            ELSE `s 52(2) the act or omission is a prohibited act` `the act or omission impairs the efficiency or impedes the working of any vessel, vehicle, aircraft, machinery, apparatus or other thing` `the act or omission causes property, by whomever it may be owned, to be lost, damaged or destroyed`

@ref Criminal Code s 52(1) (punishment) (src:902-903)
`s 52(1) the class of the offence of sabotage` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- The summary limb states no penalty: s 787(1)'s general penalty is the seam input.
@ref Criminal Code s 52(1) (punishment) (src:902-903)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 52(1) the punishment for sabotage` MEANS
    LIST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`), `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

§ `Section 52.1 -- Sabotage, essential infrastructure`

-- Subsection (2): "essential infrastructure means a facility or system, whether public or private, completed or under construction, that provides or distributes - or is intended to provide or
-- distribute - services that are essential to the health, safety, security or economic well-being of persons in Canada, including the following: (a) ... (h); and (i) any other infrastructure
-- prescribed by regulations." The listed kinds illustrate ("including"); paragraph (i) hands the question to regulations outside the sources (a seam input).
-- src:924 | Definition of essential infrastructure
-- src:925 | (2) In this section, essential infrastructure means a facility or system, whether public or private, completed or under construction, that provides or distributes — or is intended to provide or distribute — services that are essential to the health, safety, security or economic well-being of persons in Canada, including the following:
-- src:926 | (a) transportation infrastructure;
-- src:927 | (b) information and communication technology infrastructure;
-- src:928 | (c) water and wastewater management infrastructure;
-- src:929 | (d) energy and utilities infrastructure;
-- src:930 | (e) health services infrastructure;
-- src:931 | (f) food supply and food services infrastructure;
-- src:932 | (g) government operations infrastructure;
-- src:933 | (h) financial infrastructure; and
-- src:934 | (i) any other infrastructure prescribed by regulations.
@ref Criminal Code s 52.1(2) (definition of essential infrastructure) (src:924-934)
DECLARE `s 52.1(2) kind of infrastructure` IS ONE OF
    `s 52.1(2)(a) transportation infrastructure`
    `s 52.1(2)(b) information and communication technology infrastructure`
    `s 52.1(2)(c) water and wastewater management infrastructure`
    `s 52.1(2)(d) energy and utilities infrastructure`
    `s 52.1(2)(e) health services infrastructure`
    `s 52.1(2)(f) food supply and food services infrastructure`
    `s 52.1(2)(g) government operations infrastructure`
    `s 52.1(2)(h) financial infrastructure`
    `s 52.1(2) infrastructure of another kind`

@ref Criminal Code s 52.1(2) (definition of essential infrastructure) (src:924-934)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 52.1(2) kind of infrastructure`
      `it is a facility or system, whether public or private, completed or under construction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it provides or distributes, or is intended to provide or distribute, services that are essential to the health, safety, security or economic well-being of persons in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 52.1(2)(i) it is infrastructure prescribed by regulations under subsection (6)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 52.1(2) the facility or system is an essential infrastructure` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 52.1(2)(i) it is infrastructure prescribed by regulations under subsection (6)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `it is a facility or system, whether public or private, completed or under construction` AND `it provides or distributes, or is intended to provide or distribute, services that are essential to the health, safety, security or economic well-being of persons in Canada` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF kind EQUALS `s 52.1(2) infrastructure of another kind` AND `s 52.1(2)(i) it is infrastructure prescribed by regulations under subsection (6)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "essential infrastructure means a facility or system"
        IF kind EQUALS `s 52.1(2) infrastructure of another kind` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "(i) any other infrastructure prescribed by regulations" (the regulations are not among the sources)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "including the following": a listed kind that does not meet the general test is not answered by the text

-- Subsection (1): interferes with access to, or causes to be lost, inoperable, unsafe or unfit for use, an essential infrastructure with the intent to (a) endanger the safety, security or defence of
-- Canada; (b) endanger the safety or security of the naval, army or air forces of a state other than Canada lawfully present in Canada; or (c) cause a serious risk to the health or safety of the public.
-- Subsections (3) and (4) say "No person commits an offence under subsection (1) by reason only that ..." and (5) "For greater certainty, no person commits an offence ..."
