-- src:943 | (5) For greater certainty, no person commits an offence under subsection (1) if they interfere with access to an essential infrastructure or cause an essential infrastructure to be lost, inoperable, unsafe or unfit for use while participating in advocacy, protest or dissent but they do not intend to cause any of the harms referred to in paragraphs (1)(a) to (c).
@ref Criminal Code s 52.1(1) and (3) to (5) (sabotage, essential infrastructure) (src:919-943)
GIVEN `the person interferes with access to an essential infrastructure, or causes it to be lost, inoperable, unsafe or unfit for use` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 52.1(2) the facility or system is an essential infrastructure: the answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person intends to endanger the safety, security or defence of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person intends to endanger the safety or security of the naval, army or air forces of a state other than Canada that are lawfully present in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person intends to cause a serious risk to the health or safety of the public or any segment of the public` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the only reason for the offence is that the person stops work as a result of the failure of the person and their employer to agree on any matter relating to their employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the only reason for the offence is that the person stops work as a result of the failure of the person's employer and a bargaining agent acting on the person's behalf to agree` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the only reason for the offence is that the person stops work as a result of taking part in a combination of workers or employees for their own reasonable protection` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the only reason for the offence is that the person attends at or near or approaches a dwelling-house or place for the purpose only of obtaining or communicating information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person does the act while participating in advocacy, protest or dissent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 52.1(1) the person commits sabotage of an essential infrastructure` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the only reason for the offence is that the person stops work as a result of the failure of the person and their employer to agree on any matter relating to their employment`
            OR `the only reason for the offence is that the person stops work as a result of the failure of the person's employer and a bargaining agent acting on the person's behalf to agree`
            OR `the only reason for the offence is that the person stops work as a result of taking part in a combination of workers or employees for their own reasonable protection`
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person commits an offence under subsection (1) by reason only that (a) they stop work as a result of the failure of their employer and themselves to agree" (subsection (3)(a) to (c))
        IF `the only reason for the offence is that the person attends at or near or approaches a dwelling-house or place for the purpose only of obtaining or communicating information` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person commits an offence under subsection (1) by reason only that they attend at or near or approach a dwelling-house or place for the purpose only of obtaining or communicating information"
        IF `the person interferes with access to an essential infrastructure, or causes it to be lost, inoperable, unsafe or unfit for use` AND `the person does the act while participating in advocacy, protest or dissent` AND (NOT `an intent to cause one of the harms`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no person commits an offence under subsection (1) if they interfere with access to an essential infrastructure or cause an essential infrastructure to be lost, inoperable, unsafe or unfit for use while participating in advocacy, protest or dissent but they do not intend to cause any of the harms"
        IF `s 52.1(2) the facility or system is an essential infrastructure: the answer` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "essential infrastructure means a facility or system"
        IF `the person interferes with access to an essential infrastructure, or causes it to be lost, inoperable, unsafe or unfit for use` AND `s 52.1(2) the facility or system is an essential infrastructure: the answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `an intent to cause one of the harms` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "who interferes with access to an essential infrastructure or causes an essential infrastructure to be lost, inoperable, unsafe or unfit for use with the intent to"
    WHERE
        `an intent to cause one of the harms` MEANS
                `the person intends to endanger the safety, security or defence of Canada`
            OR  `the person intends to endanger the safety or security of the naval, army or air forces of a state other than Canada that are lawfully present in Canada`
            OR  `the person intends to cause a serious risk to the health or safety of the public or any segment of the public`

@ref Criminal Code s 52.1(1) (punishment) (src:919-920)
`s 52.1(1) the class of the offence of sabotage of an essential infrastructure` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

@ref Criminal Code s 52.1(1) (punishment) (src:919-920)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 52.1(1) the punishment for sabotage of an essential infrastructure` MEANS
    LIST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`), `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

§ `Section 52.2 -- Sabotage, device`

-- Subsection (3): "For the purposes of this section, device includes a computer program as defined in subsection 342.1(2)". "Includes" and the word "device" is otherwise undefined: a thing the
-- person says is a device in the ordinary sense counts as asked, a computer program (borrowed from s 342.1(2): a seam input) counts by the text, and anything else is NOTHING.
-- src:952 | Definition of device
-- src:953 | (3) For the purposes of this section, device includes a computer program as defined in subsection 342.1(2).
@ref Criminal Code s 52.2(3) (definition of device) (src:952-953)
GIVEN `the thing is a device in the ordinary sense of the word` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 342.1(2) the thing is a computer program` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 52.2(3) the thing is a device` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 342.1(2) the thing is a computer program` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the thing is a device in the ordinary sense of the word` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "device includes a computer program as defined in subsection 342.1(2)" (the text does not otherwise say what a device is)

-- src:946 | Sabotage — device
-- src:947 | 52.2 (1) Every person commits an offence who makes, possesses, sells or distributes a device intending that it be used or knowing that it will be used, in whole or in part, to carry out an offence under subsection 52(1) or 52.1(1).
@ref Criminal Code s 52.2(1) (sabotage, device) (src:946-947)
GIVEN `the person makes, possesses, sells or distributes the thing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 52.2(3) the thing is a device: the answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person intends that it be used, in whole or in part, to carry out an offence under subsection 52(1) or 52.1(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows that it will be used, in whole or in part, to carry out an offence under subsection 52(1) or 52.1(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 52.2(1) the person commits the device offence` MEANS
    IF `the person makes, possesses, sells or distributes the thing` AND `s 52.2(3) the thing is a device: the answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        AND (`the person intends that it be used, in whole or in part, to carry out an offence under subsection 52(1) or 52.1(1)` OR `the person knows that it will be used, in whole or in part, to carry out an offence under subsection 52(1) or 52.1(1)`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person commits an offence who makes, possesses, sells or distributes a device intending that it be used or knowing that it will be used"

-- src:948 | Punishment
-- src:949 | (2) Every person who commits an offence under subsection (1)
-- src:950 | (a) is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years; or
-- src:951 | (b) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 52.2(2) (punishment) (src:948-951)
`s 52.2(2) the class of the offence under subsection 52.2(1)` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

@ref Criminal Code s 52.2(2) (punishment) (src:948-951)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 52.2(2) the punishment for an offence under subsection 52.2(1)` MEANS
    LIST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`), `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

§ `Section 52.3 -- Attorney General's consent`

-- "No proceeding for an offence under subsection 52(1), 52.1(1) or 52.2(1) shall be instituted without the Attorney General's consent." A flat negative with a gate ("without"): with no consent the
-- bar holds (JUST TRUE); with consent the bar is not engaged but the text does not say the proceeding may go ahead (NOTHING: limited by its own wording).
-- src:954 | Attorney General’s consent
-- src:955 | 52.3 No proceeding for an offence under subsection 52(1), 52.1(1) or 52.2(1) shall be instituted without the Attorney General’s consent.
@ref Criminal Code s 52.3 (Attorney General's consent) (src:954-955)
GIVEN `the offence is one under subsection 52(1), 52.1(1) or 52.2(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney General has consented to the proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 52.3 the proceeding is barred without the Attorney General's consent` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the offence is one under subsection 52(1), 52.1(1) or 52.2(1)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for an offence under subsection 52(1), 52.1(1) or 52.2(1)"
        IF `the Attorney General has consented to the proceeding` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without the Attorney General's consent"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Sections 53 to 56 -- Inciting to mutiny, assisting deserter, overt acts, members of the R.C.M.P.`

-- src:956 | Inciting to mutiny
-- src:957 | 53 Every one who
-- src:958 | (a) attempts, for a traitorous or mutinous purpose, to seduce a member of the Canadian Forces from his duty and allegiance to Her Majesty, or
-- src:959 | (b) attempts to incite or to induce a member of the Canadian Forces to commit a traitorous or mutinous act,
-- src:960 | is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding fourteen years.
@ref Criminal Code s 53 (inciting to mutiny) (src:956-960)
DECLARE `s 53 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 53(a) attempts, for a traitorous or mutinous purpose, to seduce a member of the Canadian Forces from his duty and allegiance to Her Majesty`
    `s 53(b) attempts to incite or to induce a member of the Canadian Forces to commit a traitorous or mutinous act`
    `s 53 an act that is neither of those in paragraphs (a) and (b)`

@ref Criminal Code s 53 (inciting to mutiny) (src:956-960)
GIVEN act IS A `s 53 act`
      `the attempt is for a traitorous or mutinous purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2 Canadian Forces: the person is a member of the Canadian Forces` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 53 the person incites to mutiny` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 2 Canadian Forces: the person is a member of the Canadian Forces` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND act EQUALS `s 53(a) attempts, for a traitorous or mutinous purpose, to seduce a member of the Canadian Forces from his duty and allegiance to Her Majesty` AND `the attempt is for a traitorous or mutinous purpose` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 2 Canadian Forces: the person is a member of the Canadian Forces` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND act EQUALS `s 53(b) attempts to incite or to induce a member of the Canadian Forces to commit a traitorous or mutinous act` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a member of the Canadian Forces", "for a traitorous or mutinous purpose"

@ref Criminal Code s 53 (punishment) (src:956-960)
`s 53 the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

@ref Criminal Code s 53 (punishment) (src:956-960)
`s 53 the punishment` MEANS
    LIST Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

-- src:961 | Assisting deserter
-- src:962 | 54 Every one who aids, assists, harbours or conceals a person who he knows is a deserter or absentee without leave from the Canadian Forces is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction, but no proceedings shall be instituted under this section without the consent of the Attorney General of Canada.
@ref Criminal Code s 54 (assisting deserter) (src:961-962)
GIVEN `the person aids, assists, harbours or conceals another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows the other is a deserter or absentee without leave from the Canadian Forces` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 54 the person assists a deserter` MEANS
    IF `the person aids, assists, harbours or conceals another person` AND `the person knows the other is a deserter or absentee without leave from the Canadian Forces`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every one who aids, assists, harbours or conceals a person who he knows is a deserter or absentee without leave from the Canadian Forces"

@ref Criminal Code s 54 (the offence is punishable on summary conviction) (src:961-962)
`s 54 the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- The penalty is not stated here: s 787(1) is the seam input.
@ref Criminal Code s 54 (punishment) (src:961-962)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 54 the punishment` MEANS LIST `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

@ref Criminal Code s 54 (consent of the Attorney General of Canada) (src:961-962)
GIVEN `the proceedings are instituted under section 54` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney General of Canada has consented to the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 54 the proceedings are barred without the consent of the Attorney General of Canada` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the proceedings are instituted under section 54` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "no proceedings shall be instituted under this section"
        IF `the Attorney General of Canada has consented to the proceedings` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without the consent of the Attorney General of Canada"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- Section 55: "In proceedings for an offence against any provision in section 47 or sections 50 to 53, evidence of an overt act is not admissible unless that overt act is set out in the indictment or
-- unless the evidence is otherwise relevant as tending to prove an overt act that is set out in the indictment." The offence charged is tested by its section number (PLAN.md seam rule R1);
-- "section 47" is the text's own wording and is applied as written; "sections 50 to 53" is every section number from 50 to 53 in the Code's order (so 52.1 and 52.2 are within it).
-- src:963 | Evidence of overt acts
-- src:964 | 55 In proceedings for an offence against any provision in section 47 or sections 50 to 53, evidence of an overt act is not admissible unless that overt act is set out in the indictment or unless the evidence is otherwise relevant as tending to prove an overt act that is set out in the indictment.
@ref Criminal Code s 55 (evidence of overt acts) (src:963-964)
GIVEN `the offence charged` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the overt act is set out in the indictment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the evidence is otherwise relevant as tending to prove an overt act that is set out in the indictment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 55 evidence of an overt act is not admissible` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the offence charged is against section 47 or sections 50 to 53` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for an offence against any provision in section 47 or sections 50 to 53"
        IF `the overt act is set out in the indictment` OR `the evidence is otherwise relevant as tending to prove an overt act that is set out in the indictment` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless that overt act is set out in the indictment or unless the evidence is otherwise relevant as tending to prove an overt act that is set out in the indictment"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `the offence charged is against section 47 or sections 50 to 53` MEANS
                `the offence charged`'s `section` EQUALS 47
            OR  (`the offence charged`'s `section` AT LEAST 50 AND `the offence charged`'s `section` AT MOST 53)

-- src:965 | Offences in relation to members of R.C.M.P.
-- src:966 | 56 Every one who wilfully
-- src:967 | (a) persuades or counsels a member of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police to desert or absent himself without leave,
-- src:968 | (b) aids, assists, harbours or conceals a member of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police who he knows is a deserter or absentee without leave, or
-- src:969 | (c) aids or assists a member of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police to desert or absent himself without leave, knowing that the member is about to desert or absent himself without leave,
-- src:970 | is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 56 (offences in relation to members of the R.C.M.P.) (src:965-970)
DECLARE `s 56 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 56(a) persuades or counsels a member of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police to desert or absent himself without leave`
    `s 56(b) aids, assists, harbours or conceals a member of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police who he knows is a deserter or absentee without leave`
    `s 56(c) aids or assists a member of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police to desert or absent himself without leave, knowing that the member is about to desert or absent himself without leave`
    `s 56 an act that is none of those in paragraphs (a) to (c)`

@ref Criminal Code s 56 (offences in relation to members of the R.C.M.P.) (src:965-970)
GIVEN act IS A `s 56 act`
      `the person acts wilfully` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows the member is a deserter or absentee without leave (paragraph (b)) or is about to desert or absent himself without leave (paragraph (c))` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 56 the person commits an offence in relation to a member of the R.C.M.P.` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person acts wilfully` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every one who wilfully"
        IF act EQUALS `s 56(a) persuades or counsels a member of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police to desert or absent himself without leave` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF act EQUALS `s 56(b) aids, assists, harbours or conceals a member of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police who he knows is a deserter or absentee without leave` AND `the person knows the member is a deserter or absentee without leave (paragraph (b)) or is about to desert or absent himself without leave (paragraph (c))` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF act EQUALS `s 56(c) aids or assists a member of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police to desert or absent himself without leave, knowing that the member is about to desert or absent himself without leave` AND `the person knows the member is a deserter or absentee without leave (paragraph (b)) or is about to desert or absent himself without leave (paragraph (c))` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "Every one who wilfully (a) ... (b) ... or (c) ..." names three acts and does not close the list

@ref Criminal Code s 56 (the offence is punishable on summary conviction) (src:965-970)
`s 56 the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- The penalty is not stated here: s 787(1) is the seam input.
@ref Criminal Code s 56 (punishment) (src:965-970)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 56 the punishment` MEANS LIST `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`
